 "notes": [
  "Both hophal attestations (Deut.5.9, Deut.13.3) are the negated 'you/we shall not serve them' formula and read as plain active 'serve', not passive 'be enslaved' -- gloss follows the attested sense rather than the expected hophal passive, since the WLC's own morphological tagging (not a pipeline error) places these under hophal despite the active meaning."
